  steps:
    - Pick grid size 10-12 x 10-11
    - Choose 3 distinct non-bg colors for sprite_c1, sprite_c2, marker_color
    - Build a 3x3 sprite patch with sprite_c1 and sprite_c2, no bg, verify it is asymmetric under all rot90 k=1,2,3
    - Pick src_corner and dst_corner (two distinct corners from NW/NE/SW/SE)
    - Compute rotation k that maps src to dst; the OUTPUT sprite is the patch as-is
    - Compute the INPUT sprite as rot90(patch, 4-k) (inverse rotation)
    - Place sprite so all margins >= 3 (need >=2 for L-group side, >=1 for singleton, but use >=3 for safety)
    - Place L-group 3 markers around dst corner of the INPUT sprite position
    - Place singleton marker at diag-outside of src corner of the INPUT sprite position
    - Verify all 4 markers and sprite are within bounds and on background
